<title>USA: Power Control Q1 March 30 net rises.</title>
<headline>Power Control Q1 March 30 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>					     Three Months Periods Ended</p>
<p>						   Mar 30,	Mar 31,</p>
<p>						     1997	    1996</p>
<p> Net sales				     $  27.2	     --</p>
<p> Net income					  5.5	    4.7</p>
<p>Income per common share:</p>
<p> Continuing operations			  0.25	     --</p>
<p> Discontinued operations			  --	   0.21</p>
<p>  Net income					0.25	   0.21</p>
<p>Fully diluted income per common share:</p>
<p> Continuing operations			  0.24	     --</p>
<p> Discontinued operations			  --	   0.20</p>
<p>  Net income					0.24	   0.20</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said Q1 1997 includes results from its acquisition of Mafco Worldwide Corp in November 1996.</p>
<p>The company said that prior to the acquisition it did not have operations since the sale of its aerospace business in April 1996; results of the business, until April 1996, are presented as discontinued operations.</p>
<p>Full name is Power Control Technologies Inc.</p>
